{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner answer to 99fdf485. Observed query, ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-02-hosted-stream-counts, SHA256SUMS b0414d5f.\n\nDataset `artroom_metrics_v1`, points with kind `stream`, 30-day window, run at about 01:00 EST on 2 November.\n\n- Only dap-demo holds such points: 47 stored points, 105 by sample weight, from 17:19 UTC on 1 November to 02:55 UTC on 2 November. So the sink holds no earlier stream point, and none from dap-grow or dap-lending. I have no explanation for that start. Either nothing opened a stream, or points before it are gone.\n- 8 scopes, grouped by `index1`. The largest open count at any point is 4. The largest released count is 5.\n- 27 of the 47 points show a released count above 0. So hosted release does occur. 7 of the 8 scopes show a release.\n- One scope, `sc_d6altjz4xr6`, shows open 4 and released 0 in 6 points. I read that as too few samples to call a leak.\n\nLimits: the sink samples, with sample intervals up to 5, so a maximum can be missed. The counts are per object run, so a restart resets them, and I did not measure that. I read the double columns as open and released from source order, and the values fit that.\n\nRuling: nothing here shows the local 64-open, zero-released state on a deployed Worker, so the existing queue continues. Actor chip c6ced04f goes on, and 01e2c4c4 stays after the current queue items. The hosted status 200 stream ending stays with it. Move it up if a hosted scope's open count passes 20 at any survey read.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}